1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,550
This is the live Crypto Bot app.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,570
Once a day it decides whether to hold Bitcoin,

3
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:08,195
Ethereum and Solana, or wait in dollars.

4
00:00:08,245 --> 00:00:09,770
I'll start it on Solana.

5
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:12,724
With my own wallet, it would sign real swaps.

6
00:00:12,774 --> 00:00:16,531
Here I'll pick simulation: real Jupiter quotes and routes,

7
00:00:16,581 --> 00:00:17,975
virtual USDC, no risk.

8
00:00:18,775 --> 00:00:21,310
Within seconds it makes its first decision.

9
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:24,496
Each coin is above three of its four moving averages,

10
00:00:24,546 --> 00:00:26,479
so the bot holds a quarter of the

11
00:00:26,529 --> 00:00:29,064
capital in each and keeps the rest in USDC.

12
00:00:29,114 --> 00:00:31,769
The feed explains every trade in plain words,

13
00:00:31,819 --> 00:00:34,775
and the next decision comes after the daily close.

14
00:00:35,575 --> 00:00:37,728
Advanced mode shows the reasoning.

15
00:00:37,778 --> 00:00:41,616
For every coin: the daily close, its distance to the 20, 50,

16
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:44,661
100 and 200-day averages, and the target share.

17
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:46,929
Today each coin is below its 20-day

18
00:00:46,979 --> 00:00:49,132
average and above the other three.

19
00:00:49,182 --> 00:00:53,279
Below are the venue and on-chain settings, the decision journal,

20
00:00:53,329 --> 00:00:56,000
and a live log of everything the bot does.

21
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:57,863
For more history,

22
00:00:57,913 --> 00:01:00,088
here is the same app replaying the

23
00:01:00,138 --> 00:01:02,901
strategy on real 2026 prices since January.

24
00:01:02,951 --> 00:01:04,865
It is up about twelve percent,

25
00:01:04,915 --> 00:01:08,595
while simply holding the three coins lost about fourteen.

26
00:01:08,645 --> 00:01:10,427
Past prices, not a forecast.

27
00:01:10,477 --> 00:01:14,550
The interface also switches to Russian and Armenian on the fly.

28
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:17,331
The equity curve marks every trade,

29
00:01:17,381 --> 00:01:19,188
and the drawdown panel shows how

30
00:01:19,238 --> 00:01:21,219
far the capital fell from its peak:

31
00:01:21,269 --> 00:01:23,017
under twenty percent this year.

32
00:01:23,067 --> 00:01:25,396
When the trends came back in late summer,

33
00:01:25,446 --> 00:01:26,731
the bot bought back in.

34
00:01:26,781 --> 00:01:29,400
The journal filters trades, checks and errors.

35
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:33,173
Back to the live session.

36
00:01:33,223 --> 00:01:34,574
Stopping is one button:

37
00:01:34,624 --> 00:01:37,681
the bot sells everything back to USDC and shows the

38
00:01:37,731 --> 00:01:41,458
result next to what simply holding the coins would have given.

39
00:01:41,508 --> 00:01:44,991
Crypto Bot: one slow decision a day, from your own wallet,

40
00:01:45,041 --> 00:01:45,600
on Solana.
